			<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><object classid="clsid:d27cdb6e-ae6d-11cf-96b8-444553540000" width="400" height="300" codebase="http://download.macromedia.com/pub/shockwave/cabs/flash/swflash.cab#version=6,0,40,0"><param name="allowfullscreen" value="true" /><param name="allowscriptaccess" value="always" /><param name="src" value="http://vimeo.com/moogaloop.swf?clip_id=6931449&amp;server=vimeo.com&amp;show_title=1&amp;show_byline=1&amp;show_portrait=0&amp;color=&amp;fullscreen=1" /><embed type="application/x-shockwave-flash" width="400" height="300" src="http://vimeo.com/moogaloop.swf?clip_id=6931449&amp;server=vimeo.com&amp;show_title=1&amp;show_byline=1&amp;show_portrait=0&amp;color=&amp;fullscreen=1" allowscriptaccess="always" allowfullscreen="true"></embed></object></p>
<p><a href="http://vimeo.com/6931449">Shabazz Palaces &#8211; &#8220;Belhaven Meridian&#8221; [OFFICIAL]</a> from <a href="http://vimeo.com/user2412786">Kahlil Joseph</a> on <a href="http://vimeo.com">Vimeo</a>.</p>
<p>check out the latest visuals from <strong><a href="http://www.shabazzpalaces.com/">Shabazz Palaces</a></strong>, a new project by Ishmael Butler (bk to some as &#8220;<strong><a href="http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZY0c2ZAeMK4">Butterfly</a></strong>&#8220;) + art direction by the homie Maikoiyo.</p>
<p>its stated intention is to be a short film / music video done partly in homage to Charles Burnett&#8217;s &#8220;<strong><a href="http://www.killerofsheep.com/">Killer of Sheep</a></strong>.&#8221;  (you can peep an <strong><a href="http://prometheusbrown.com/blog/2008/08/killer-of-sheep-charles-burnett-1977/">old Pro Brown review here</a></strong>)</p>
<p>good to see folks trying to innovate and bring deeper meaning to the artform.</p>
